Company Description
Orchestrate data-driven transformations at our top-tier clients and help them to successfully manage data and unlock value from data assets. At Deloitte.

Job Description
Defining clients’ data strategy, business case and roadmap to ensure data is managed and used as a valuable asset;
defining a client’s ‘to-be’ state, which will involve the design of data governance operating model and the set-up of a data management office through which data is efficiently managed within the organization, securing its trust and accountability;
designing an end-to-end process to proactively raise and resolve data quality issues;
assessing vendors and recommending and implementing data tooling and methods to support client business strategies;
working on and managing projects to embed data operating models, data governance frameworks and data capabilities in the client organisation in a sustainable way;
applying your knowledge and experience in disrupting technologies and trends such as Artificial Intelligence, DataOps and Data Mesh;
assisting in the further development of our market leading solution and delivery offerings and help produce proposal documents to showcase our capabilities to clients;
working effectively and leading diverse teams within an inclusive team culture where people are recognised for their contribution.

Qualifications
When it comes to the technicalities of the job, you are ready for anything. At the same time, you are able to inspire and motivate the team to deliver excellent results. You dare to try new things and to keep learning, even if there are setbacks along the way. For the role of Manager Enterprise Data Management, you:
have graduated with a master’s degree, with a preference for technology-related studies such as Business Information; Management, Engineering, or Informatics;
have at least six years of relevant and demonstrable work experience;
have experience with leading client projects end to end;
demonstrate an understanding of data strategy and data governance principles and familiarity with processes, policies and any of the key technology vendor platforms;
demonstrate knowledge of data quality management, metadata and master data management principles;
have advised Chief Data Officers, with proven experience on our type of projects;
have a broad network within one or more industries;
are ambitious, commercial, and you dare to be entrepreneurial;
are a team player, and master the English language on working proficiency. The Dutch language is a nice to have.

Additional Information
Our Enterprise Data Management (EDM) team drives transformations towards a data-driven organization. We help our clients across industries to develop their long term data strategy, the processes and operating model. All with the objective to govern and manage data as a valuable asset and build the foundation to exploit exciting new opportunities that advanced analytics, AI, DataOps and automation present. We ensure a growing awareness on the importance of data management capabilities such as data governance, data quality and metadata management and help our clients to see, understand and capitalize data trends.
Did we already capture your interest? Great, since we are looking for a Manager to join us in solving our clients’ toughest technology, strategy and transformation problems from a data perspective. We combine industry experience, consulting skills and data management capabilities to  create a lasting impact that matters. Whether it is defining a data strategy, orchestrating new ways of working to govern and manage data more efficiently or implementing technology-based data solutions, we need the very best people to join and strengthen our inclusive EDM team! That is where you come in.

